From 31897238ac867955a4fae3b9b33d003c70a9e3a7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 18:16:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix: let closing sells through the kill cooldown

During a cooldown the kill gate blocked every action, including sells that
close an existing long. Let such a sell through when it can be emitted:
position > 0, not a repeat of the last emitted action, and no open strategy
intent on the symbol. The open-intent lookup is Codex's human-accepted
IntentQueueSQLite.has_open_strategy_intent SQL query. Entries, adds and sells
without a position stay blocked; the cooldown keeps counting.

Review: bounded re-review and human acceptance recorded in the work log.
Does not fix the multi-symbol loop. Not deployed.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
