 # Review Stabilized Work Log
 
+## 2026-10-02 - Let closing sells through the kill cooldown
+
+- ENGINEER (Claude, separate thread). Builds on the kill-cooldown expiry change
+  (entry below); separate change, separate review. Codex's local review showed
+  the kill gate also suppresses protective exits, on base and patched code.
+- Change: when the kill gate blocks a loop, a sell that closes an existing long
+  is let through, but only if it can actually be emitted: position > 0, not the
+  same action as the last emitted one, and no queued/submitted strategy intent
+  for the symbol (an unreadable intent queue counts as blocked). Entries, adds
+  to a position and sells without a position stay blocked. The cooldown still
+  counts down on every blocked or pass-through loop. No behaviour change when
+  no cooldown is active.
+- Reviewer subagent returned ACCEPT_WITH_RISK on the first draft and reproduced
+  that exit bookkeeping (loss streak, cumulative PnL, kill re-arm) runs before
+  the open-intent check, so a pass-through sell blocked by an open intent
+  repeated it every loop. The open-intent and last-emitted conditions were
+  added for that and are pinned by tests; they have not been re-reviewed.
+- Codex's local review reproduced that the open-intent check read only the
+  newest 200 intents. Codex's correction, human-accepted on 2026-10-02
+  (`docs/review_artifacts/20261002_intent_lookup/accepted_lookup_correction.patch`,
+  SHA256 prefix 051e9aa861010d35), is applied here unchanged:
+  `IntentQueueSQLite.has_open_strategy_intent`, a SQL existence query on
+  source, symbol and open status. Claude's alternative paginated helper
+  (bundle rev7) is withdrawn and not included. The inherited open-intent check
+  on the normal emission path still reads the newest 200 and is not changed.
+- Known limits, all inherited and not changed here: a long whose earlier exit
+  was emitted but never closed stays deduplicated (no second sell) for the
+  cooldown; a losing exit during a cooldown re-arms it to full, as it does
+  outside a cooldown; exit bookkeeping still precedes the open-intent check
+  when no cooldown is active; decision and kill logic remain outside the
+  per-symbol loop.
+- VERIFIED_ENV (cloud clone, Python 3.11.15): see commit message.
+- UNVERIFIED: Python 3.12, CI, hosts, intent consumer and fill behaviour,
+  partial fills. HIGH risk. Not pushed, not deployed.
+  READY_FOR_INDEPENDENT_REVIEW.
+
